  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BDI022N Turikumwe &apos;implementation level&apos;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual and reproductive health and gender-related violence are major issues in Burundi. Problems regarding sexual and reproductive health are numerous; for example, there is often a lack of informed decision-making regarding contraception and childbirth, particularly among adolescents and young people, resulting in undesired pregnancies, teenage motherhood and (too young) parents struggling with taking care of their children. CARE Burundi has been working on this theme for several years, with support from the Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in Burundi. Turikumwe 1 aims to consolidate the results already achieved so far. The geographical focus of Turikumwe 1 is the newly (since 2025) created province of Butanyerera. In addition, the program aims to eradicate Gender-Based Violence in the same intervention area.
CARE Burundi will partner directly with AJEBUDI Yaga, and Twitezimbere and other WLO and YLOs. Other stakeholders, awarded with a grant from the EKN are UNICEF, UNFPA, IPAS, Alfajiri and DKT. CARE Burundi aligns its program with them as well.</narrative>
  </description>
